### Multiple Chat Messages - Follow-up Questions
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/career/chat/{{sessionId}} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "What universities in Pakistan offer the best programs for my recommended degree?"
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/career/chat/{{sessionId}} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "What are the typical salary expectations for fresh graduates in this field?"
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/career/chat/{{sessionId}} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "How can I prepare for interviews in this field?"
}

###
# ========== ERROR HANDLING TESTS ==========
###

### Invalid User ID Format
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/career/profile HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "",
  "answers": {}
}

### Missing Required Answers
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/career/profile HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "test_user",
  "answers": {
    "q1": "bachelors"
  }
}

### Invalid Session ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/career/session/invalid_session_id_123 HTTP/1.1

### Empty Chat Message
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/career/chat/{{sessionId}} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": ""
}

### Non-existent Endpoint (404 Test)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/career/nonexistent HTTP/1.1

###
# ========== RATE LIMITING TESTS ==========
###

### Rapid Fire Requests (Test Rate Limiter)
# Execute these 6 times rapidly to trigger rate limiting
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/career/recommend HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}"
}

###
# ========== INSTRUCTIONS ==========
# 
# 1. Install REST Client extension in VS Code
# 2. Ensure server is running: npm run dev
# 3. Replace {{userId}} with an actual user ID after first profile submission
# 4. Replace {{sessionId}} with actual session ID from recommendation response
# 5. For AI recommendations (step 5), ensure OPENAI_API_KEY is set in .env
# 6. Click "Send Request" above any ### line to execute that request
# 7. View responses in the right panel
#
# Expected Flow:
# Step 3 → Get questions
# Step 4 → Submit profile (save the userId from response)
# Step 5 → Generate recommendations (save the sessionId from response)
# Step 6-10 → Use the sessionId for subsequent requests
###
